{"id": "623d8a4242cd9e7b1ed7c8d5", "name": "Arid Gopher Malware Targets Computers Running Microsoft Windows to Infiltrate Important Assets", "description": "Researchers found a Go-written variant of the malware in 2017 named it Arid Gopher. It is used exclusively by Arid Viper (aka APT-C-23), an APT group believed to be based in Gaza.\n\n'helper' and second-stage malware\nThis new variant is still being developed; all three files share a common baseline, but each file contains unique code which is not present in the other files. Besides the main implant, a 'helper' malware, and a second-stage malware that was downloaded from the C2 server were also written in Go.", "author_name": "SVThreatIntel", "modified": "2022-03-25T09:24:18.910000", "created": "2022-03-25T09:24:18.910000", "tags": ["archive", "iocs sha256", "aridgopher v2", "v1 c2", "Arid Gopher Malware", "Microsoft"], "references": ["https://www.deepinstinct.com/blog/arid-gopher-the-newest-micropsia-malware-variant"], "public": 1, "adversary": "Malware Advisory", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "indicators": [{"id": 3405948931, "indicator": "1f7c854e05be627776d27370bcdc082c", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-03-25T09:24:19", "content": "", "title": "Arid Gopher", "description": "MD5 of 5588f6fab387133c21b06f6248259c64260435898edd61866fad50312c2d3b25", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3405948932, "indicator": "22a1278d4dadc420166fbbdafa543bb1", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-03-25T09:24:19", "content": "", "title": "GoLandBuildPE", "description": "MD5 of 3d7d75d66428c55dc81563c3bde5477977fadb3325d0224ef9313da133940077", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3405948934, "indicator": "747fb6974716c2649ba912b578ffc7d4", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-03-25T09:24:19", "content": "", "title": "RAR_Archive", "description": "MD5 of f01c07f88071c8f71514db19f68c966f17ac8af0d3288913141714037352c99c", "expira